  "name": "Example: Simplifying Expressions Containing Cube Root Surds",
  "problem": "Find $\\sqrt[3]{12} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Grouping up the square roots and the cube roots, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{12}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12} & = \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{12}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12})(\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}) & = \\\\ {(\\sqrt[3]{12})}^{3}{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2} & = \\\\ 12\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ 36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
